    "parsing_res_list": [
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "where $\\odot$ denotes the Hadamard (or element-wise) matrix product. Fixing $\\boldsymbol{v}$, the pure-coskewness update for $\\boldsymbol{w}$ is the leading eigenvector of the $p\\times p$ matrix $\\boldsymbol{A}(u)=\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}\\operatorname{diag}(u)\\boldsymbol{X}/n$, obtained by power iteration through the matrix-free product $\\boldsymbol{A}(u)\\boldsymbol{z}=\\boldsymbol{X}^{\\top}[u\\odot(\\boldsymbol{X}\\boldsymbol{z})]/n$; each step costs $O(n(p+q))$ and no $p\\times p$ matrix is ever stored. The matrix $\\boldsymbol{A}(u)$ is symmetric but indefinite, so the iteration converges to the eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue of largest magnitude. Because $\\mathbb{E}[t^{2}u]$ is odd in $\\boldsymbol{v}$, a negative dominant eigenvalue is resolved by flipping the sign of $\\boldsymbol{v}$. For the combined objective $0<\\gamma<1$ the $\\boldsymbol{w}$-update is a safeguarded normalized-gradient fixed point that ascends (5) monotonically; it reduces continuously to the covariance power method as $\\gamma\\to0$. The alternation is initialized deterministically from the covariance leading singular pair, and run from a small number of deterministic starts (the covariance warm start plus a few coordinate starts at the most promising variables). Note that this is owed to the ascent being only locally convergent. The full procedure is summarized in Algorithm 1; a soft-thresholding step (Serneels, 2025) may be applied to the converged $\\boldsymbol{w}$ to obtain sparse directions, exactly as in the covariance case.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                146,
                1094,
                552
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 0,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    146.0
                ],
                [
                    1094.0,
                    146.0
                ],
                [
                    1094.0,
                    552.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    552.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "algorithm",
            "block_content": "Algorithm 1 One coskewness direction (matrix-free HOPM), X-side loop.\n\nRequire: Centred, scaled X, Y; weight $\\gamma \\in [0,1];$ tolerances.\n\n1: Initialize $(w, v)$ from the leading singular pair of $X^{\\top}Y/n$.\n\n2: repeat\n\n3: $t \\leftarrow Xw$; update $v \\propto Y^{\\top}[(1-\\gamma)t+\\gamma(t\\odot t)]/n$, renormalize; $u \\leftarrow Yv$.\n\n4: if $\\gamma = 1$ then\n\n5: $w \\leftarrow$ dominant-magnitude eigenvector of $A(u) = X^{\\top}$diag($u$)X/n by matrix-free power iteration;\n\n6: if its Rayleigh quotient is negative, set $v \\leftarrow -v$, $u \\leftarrow -u$.\n\n7: else\n\n8: $w \\leftarrow$ safeguarded normalized-gradient fixed point of (5).\n\n9: end if\n\n10: until the objective (5) stops increasing.\n\n11: return $w$ (optionally soft-thresholded).",
            "block_bbox": [
                144,
                572,
                1084,
                986
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
