        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The population moments are decisive:  $ \\mathrm{cov}(z, y) = \\mathbb{E}[z^3] = 0 $ while  $ \\mathbb{E}[z^2 y] = \\mathbb{E}[z^4] - \\mathbb{E}[z^2] = 2 $. The covariance objective is thus unable to rank the planted direction  $ z $ above the decoy  $ x_2 $,",
